 (a folder named there is taken as written). Only these two count as wide: the top of a file system (`/`, or the top of a drive on Windows) and your home folder. Any other folder you start in, even a broad one such as `/home`, `/Users`, `/usr` or `/etc`, is allowed as written, so start the tool in a project folder. The same rule applies to `scripts/n8n_api.py import FILE` and `tools/scrub_n8n_export.py` (an n8n export kept in another folder, for example Downloads, is read after you copy it into the repository folder or list its folder in `LEAD_DESK_PATH_ROOTS`).
 
 Not covered, on purpose: `scripts/run_real_check.py` reads its config from any folder (the documentation tells you to keep it outside the repository) and uses the paths named inside it as written, and `scripts/run_live_check.py` takes its key file and its spend ledger from any folder for the same reason (`docs/real-services.md`). The config of `run_real_check.py` is found by looking the name up in the folder listings from the top of the file system, so it must be a file in a folder you can list: a config below a folder that you can enter but not list (mode 0711 owned by another user), or one handed over as `--config <(command)`, `/dev/fd/N` or `/dev/stdin` when it is a pipe (`/dev/stdin` redirected from a file works), is refused with a message; copy it to a normal file first. On macOS (upper and lower case are the same on disk) every folder of the config path must be typed in the case the file system reports, or the config is refused as "no such file". What this check is: a fence against a WRONG argument (a faulty script, a copied path). It is not a defence against an agent or a person who controls the shell: they can start the tool in another folder or set `LEAD_DESK_PATH_ROOTS`. The allowed folders are wide, and a file that already exists in one of them (the repository, the shared system temporary folder) can be overwritten by an output option that names it: the check does not know which files in them matter. It does not stop another process that swaps a folder for a link between the check and the open. The tools also start directly (`python load_tools/load_driver.py --help`, `python tools/scrub_n8n_export.py in.json out.json`) without setting `PYTHONPATH`.
 
